son means "son of Harry".","title":"Harrison (name)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Early records suggest that the surnames Harrison and Harris were used interchangeably by some families.","title":"Harrison (name)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Harrison is the 42nd most common surname in England and 123rd most common in the United States.","title":"Harrison (name)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The surname was first recorded in 1355, in London, England.","title":"Harrison (name)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The André Baronetcy, of Southampton in the County of Southampton, was a title in the Baronetage of Great Britain.","title":"André baronets"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was created on 4 March 1781 for William André, in recognition of the services rendered to the country by his brother John André, who was executed in 1780 after being convicted of espionage by an American tribunal during the American Revolutionary War.","title":"André baronets"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The title became extinct on William André's death in 1802.","title":"André baronets"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Kingdom of Holland (Dutch: "Koninkrijk Holland" , French: "Royaume de Hollande" ) was set up by Napoléon Bonaparte as a puppet kingdom for his third brother, Louis Bonaparte, in order to better control the Netherlands.","title":"Kingdom of Holland"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The name of the leading province, Holland, was now taken for the whole country.","title":"Kingdom of Holland"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 1807 Prussian East Frisia and Jever were added to the kingdom but in 1809, after a British invasion, Holland had to give over all territories south of the river Rhine to France.","title":"Kingdom of Holland"}],"peer_messages":["Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Rules of origin are used to determine the country of origin of a product for purposes of international trade.","title":"Rules of origin"}
